{"_id":"68a736208ec3d8323af18b49","nodeId":"N5ojp6bqgH074MPKYjCHV","roadmapSlug":"ios","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:12.170Z","description":"# Error Handling\n\nSwift provides a structured error handling model using the throw, try, and catch keywords. Functions that can fail declare throws in their signature, and callers handle errors using do-catch blocks. Swift also supports the Result type for propagating errors through asynchronous APIs.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"General Error Handling Rules - Google","url":"https://developers.google.com/tech-writing/error-messages/error-handling","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf85ff"},{"type":"article","title":"Error Handling Patterns","url":"https://andreabergia.com/blog/2023/05/error-handling-patterns/","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf8600"},{"type":"video","title":"Error Handling by Timoth Cain","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yhJEJKG-aK8","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf8601"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:04:24.838Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ios/content/N5ojp6bqgH074MPKYjCHV.md"}